Change: Update the CA bundle

The bundled CA certificates were replaced with curl's 2026-10-20 extract of
the Mozilla root store. This removes emSign ECC Root CA - G3, which anchors
eMudhra intermediate CAs whose private keys were compromised.

The update removes 35 roots in line with the Mozilla store and adds 7. The
removed roots include DigiCert Global Root CA, DigiCert Assured ID Root CA,
DigiCert High Assurance EV Root CA, the Entrust root CAs, COMODO
Certification Authority, QuoVadis Root CA 2 and 3, emSign Root CA - C1 and
emSign ECC Root CA - C3. Outgoing HTTPS connections to servers whose
certificates chain only to a removed root now fail verification. To keep
trusting such a root, import it with `occ security:certificates:import`.

